From: xtandard-image
Subject: [PATCH] Bound metadata reads

Found by libFuzzer: ReadBinaryData allocated uCount + 2 bytes for a count
read from the file (a 3.6 GB request; with uCount = 0xFFFFFFFF the sum
wraps to 1 and the read would overflow it). Refuse counts above 16 MiB.
---
--- a/jxrgluelib/JXRMeta.c
+++ b/jxrgluelib/JXRMeta.c
@@ -674,6 +674,10 @@
     ERR err = WMP_errSuccess;
     U8 *pbData = NULL;
 
+    // uCount comes from the file: + 2 must not wrap (a 1-byte buffer read
+    // into with the full count), and no metadata value is anywhere near
+    // 16 MiB.
+    FailIf(uCount > (1u << 24), WMP_errBufferOverflow);
     Call(PKAlloc((void **) &pbData, uCount + 2)); // Allocate buffer to store data with space for an added ascii or unicode null
     if (uCount <= 4)
     {
